WEBVTT

00:11.650 --> 00:14.670
Love, I've got to feel it

00:14.950 --> 00:18.000
If you put your trust in me

00:18.270 --> 00:21.520
I know what my life would be

00:21.590 --> 00:26.410
Oh, you are all I ever need

00:26.570 --> 00:32.110
I try to hear what you say

00:32.260 --> 00:34.380
So I pray

00:34.460 --> 00:37.960
But you're fading away

00:39.400 --> 00:45.120
Don't go and break my fragile heart

00:45.550 --> 00:48.750
We won't fall apart

00:48.870 --> 00:56.930
'Cause you're my only star

00:58.890 --> 01:02.640
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:02.640 --> 01:06.150
Calling you, so like a little child

01:06.310 --> 01:09.390
All the things you have in mind

01:09.650 --> 01:12.770
I wish I could see your insides

01:12.770 --> 01:15.800
My love, you've got to feel it

01:15.800 --> 01:19.110
And if we put our trust in you and me

01:19.320 --> 01:22.770
You know what our lives would be

01:22.890 --> 01:30.730
Oh, you are the one, I believe

01:43.040 --> 01:44.450
Yuko-chan?

01:47.390 --> 01:49.370
Do you know where Yu is?

01:49.850 --> 01:52.320
Oh, Himura-senpai?

01:52.320 --> 01:53.370
No, I don't.

01:53.370 --> 01:57.850
He hasn't been to school in a while,
and apparently he's not at home either.

01:57.850 --> 01:59.480
I see.

01:59.480 --> 02:02.150
I just thought that you might know something, Yuko-chan.

02:02.150 --> 02:04.340
I'm sorry. I don't.

02:04.710 --> 02:07.860
You were absent from school for a while too, weren't you?

02:07.860 --> 02:08.640
Yes.

02:10.130 --> 02:11.640
Around the same time as Yu.

02:13.850 --> 02:15.460
You don't know where Yu is?

02:15.460 --> 02:16.380
No.

02:25.110 --> 02:26.570
Do you need something?

02:26.700 --> 02:31.080
I'm bad at playing with words, so I'll be straightforward.

02:31.200 --> 02:32.950
Please don't make Yu unhappy.

02:34.200 --> 02:38.630
I say that because you're the only one who can make him unhappy.

02:55.900 --> 02:58.650
Make Himura-senpai unhappy...

02:59.270 --> 03:02.150
Isn't that exactly what I wanted?

03:02.650 --> 03:06.650
Isn't that what I had intended from the start?

03:07.670 --> 03:09.760
And yet...

03:09.760 --> 03:10.700
Why?

03:15.080 --> 03:18.710
I... didn't allow Yuko to become my little sister.

03:21.980 --> 03:27.470
I... wanted to exact revenge on Himura-senpai.

03:29.420 --> 03:33.190
I... was prepared to live alone forever.

03:35.100 --> 03:40.650
I... wanted to share my pain with him, even though he could survive by himself.

03:45.150 --> 03:47.780
I didn't sketch Yuko's portrait for her.

03:48.900 --> 03:52.530
I couldn't forget my own sister.

03:56.250 --> 03:59.710
I was envious of Himura-senpai.

04:00.280 --> 04:04.720
And such a small thing caused Yuko so much pain.

04:04.720 --> 04:09.340
And such a small thing made me hate Himura-senpai so much.

04:13.210 --> 04:15.890
That was a huge mistake.

04:17.020 --> 04:22.520
Why didn't I realize that it was a huge mistake?

04:22.520 --> 04:24.720
How can I make up for it?

04:24.720 --> 04:26.780
I shouldn't have hurt him!

04:27.040 --> 04:28.900
How can I save her?

04:28.900 --> 04:30.950
I shouldn't have gotten close to him!

04:34.990 --> 04:38.910
If only I'd noticed my own feelings sooner!

04:38.910 --> 04:42.040
If only I'd realized that I loved her sooner!

04:46.150 --> 04:49.140
If only I'd been honest from the beginning...

04:49.140 --> 04:51.580
Instead of wanting to be a sister...

04:51.580 --> 04:54.470
If I'd told him from the beginning that I loved him!

04:56.880 --> 05:01.850
I didn't think that I'd come to love him <i>this much!</i>

05:08.040 --> 05:10.110
Why?

05:18.230 --> 05:19.790
I've returned just now.

05:19.790 --> 05:21.910
Ah, welcome back.

05:26.680 --> 05:29.070
What are those wounds, Yuko?

05:32.550 --> 05:35.070
I don't remember seeing them.

05:36.010 --> 05:37.640
Did you inflict them yourself?

05:44.880 --> 05:47.150
What is this about?

05:48.400 --> 05:50.860
Are you punishing yourself?

05:50.860 --> 05:52.570
Do you feel a sense of guilt...

05:52.570 --> 05:53.360
regarding him?

05:53.630 --> 05:54.990
I'm sorry.

05:57.240 --> 05:59.310
He's the same as me.

05:59.310 --> 06:01.870
There's no reason for you to feel guilty.

06:01.870 --> 06:03.380
Understood?

06:03.380 --> 06:04.000
Yes.

06:06.920 --> 06:10.090
It's not like you've done anything wrong.

06:10.090 --> 06:13.510
It's all because of that earthquake.

06:14.270 --> 06:17.930
That earthquake stole my sister away.

06:18.190 --> 06:21.060
It took everything she had away.

06:21.060 --> 06:21.930
And yet...

06:21.930 --> 06:23.810
Why are <i>you still alive?</i>

06:24.160 --> 06:26.900
Why are <i>you, who looks exactly like her, still alive?</i>

06:26.900 --> 06:28.560
And why was <i>she the only one who died?!</i>

06:31.980 --> 06:33.240
Why...

06:33.240 --> 06:35.240
Why?!

06:35.240 --> 06:36.740
She was just unlucky.

06:37.700 --> 06:39.490
Himura-senpai!

06:39.490 --> 06:41.080
She was just unlucky.

06:41.080 --> 06:42.870
My sister...

06:42.870 --> 06:44.080
and your sister too.

06:44.080 --> 06:46.310
I know that, of course.

06:46.310 --> 06:48.750
But still...

06:48.750 --> 06:50.830
can you accept that fact?

06:50.830 --> 06:52.100
No, I can't!

06:52.100 --> 06:54.410
Even so, though we can't accept it, we <i>have to, don't we?</i>

06:54.410 --> 06:55.840
I won't accept it.

06:55.840 --> 07:00.850
Both of us will be shackled by them unendingly until we die.

07:00.850 --> 07:03.360
We're not going to be shackled by them,
we're going to carry them!

07:03.360 --> 07:05.980
I'm going to live my life carrying Akane!

07:08.920 --> 07:10.400
Go home.

07:10.400 --> 07:12.070
Please stop, Nii-san!

07:12.070 --> 07:14.530
You're just like me.

07:14.530 --> 07:15.440
No, I'm not!

07:17.530 --> 07:18.900
What's wrong?

07:18.900 --> 07:20.280
You're not going to fight back?

07:26.790 --> 07:27.910
Nii-san, please stop!

07:32.170 --> 07:35.630
You've finally decided to point that at me?

07:35.630 --> 07:37.680
Don't... Yuko!

07:37.680 --> 07:38.890
Senpai...

07:38.890 --> 07:39.820
But...

07:39.820 --> 07:40.640
Oh?

07:40.990 --> 07:43.640
Didn't you say that you'd stopped drawing?

07:44.560 --> 07:50.060
Humans are creatures unable to stop doing something they really desire.

07:50.430 --> 07:54.070
Your drawing, and my actions, are no exception.

07:54.070 --> 07:56.780
You actually like it, don't you?

07:59.490 --> 08:01.760
Why...

08:01.760 --> 08:04.120
Why in the world did you draw this?

08:04.120 --> 08:06.120
Why in the world did you draw my...

08:06.330 --> 08:07.700
This is it...

08:07.700 --> 08:08.710
This is it.

08:08.710 --> 08:10.250
This is really it!

08:14.360 --> 08:15.550
Wh-Why?

08:15.750 --> 08:17.510
After all this time, why now?

08:31.030 --> 08:33.110
Could this be...

08:33.110 --> 08:33.910
Yes.

08:33.910 --> 08:36.860
His deceased sister.

08:38.250 --> 08:39.400
This is it!

08:39.400 --> 08:40.620
This is it!

08:40.620 --> 08:41.920
It's this face!

08:41.920 --> 08:43.740
It's this expression!

08:44.030 --> 08:46.430
Why couldn't I remember it until now?

08:46.430 --> 08:48.830
Why couldn't I draw it until now?

08:48.830 --> 08:51.780
This... is Amamiya's little sister?

08:51.780 --> 08:53.000
Don't touch it!

08:53.190 --> 08:54.710
Get out.

08:55.290 --> 08:56.710
Get out of here!

09:01.090 --> 09:02.840
we

09:04.640 --> 09:07.810
Didn't Amamiya give up drawing?

09:07.810 --> 09:10.470
It's not that he gave up drawing, it's that he <i>couldn't draw.</i>

09:10.470 --> 09:11.350
Huh?

09:11.350 --> 09:16.350
Ever since that earthquake, for some reason, he just couldn't draw his sister's face.

09:16.350 --> 09:20.190
And because of that, he stopped drawing altogether.

09:20.190 --> 09:24.400
Nii-san always shuts himself away, and whenever he tries to draw,

09:24.400 --> 09:27.450
he loses heart and cries for a very long time.

09:27.450 --> 09:28.490
He does?

09:28.490 --> 09:30.080
He's a truly sad man.

09:30.080 --> 09:33.730
Then, why <i>now?</i>

09:33.730 --> 09:34.690
Senpai.

09:34.690 --> 09:35.460
Hm?

09:35.460 --> 09:37.300
That sketchbook...

09:37.300 --> 09:39.420
What did you draw in it?

09:42.620 --> 09:44.230
I wanted to see you.

09:44.250 --> 09:46.680
I wanted to see you!

09:46.680 --> 09:48.560
You were lonely, weren't you?

09:48.560 --> 09:49.870
I'm sorry

09:49.870 --> 09:51.730
for leaving you all by yourself.

09:51.730 --> 09:54.150
But everything's all right now!

09:54.150 --> 09:56.190
We'll be together forever.

10:17.450 --> 10:18.290
Amamiya!

10:18.290 --> 10:19.040
Nii-san!

10:31.430 --> 10:33.090
What the hell are you doing, Amamiya?!

10:33.090 --> 10:34.060
You'll burn to death!

10:36.060 --> 10:37.310
Amamiya!

12:45.980 --> 12:49.490
Reaching out my hand, I'm running

12:45.980 --> 12:49.490
Chasing your shadow

13:20.770 --> 13:23.190
I've settled everything.

13:23.190 --> 13:25.770
Nothing's been left unsettled.

13:25.770 --> 13:29.480
When I die, nothing will be left behind.

13:29.480 --> 13:34.200
No one will grieve, no one will cry, no one will be troubled.

13:34.200 --> 13:37.440
I'm going to quietly disappear from everyone's memories.

13:55.340 --> 13:57.550
It's all for the best, isn't it?

13:57.550 --> 13:59.560
It's exactly what I wished for.

14:01.920 --> 14:05.910
I can't make anyone happy anymore.

14:05.910 --> 14:08.940
I can't participate in something that I know I'm going to lose.

14:13.190 --> 14:16.180
All I have left is to wait for the end now.

14:16.180 --> 14:18.570
No one can wind the spring anymore.

14:22.580 --> 14:26.420
But no one can make the pendulum swing faster.

14:35.530 --> 14:40.680
There are only a few days left, but when you wait for it, it seems so long.

14:40.680 --> 14:42.680
memorable

15:02.410 --> 15:03.700
Wait... huh?

15:03.700 --> 15:06.210
Now that I think about it, this song...

15:06.670 --> 15:12.860
The courage to live, and...

15:14.710 --> 15:16.750
This is...

15:16.750 --> 15:18.470
If I remember correctly...

15:18.470 --> 15:21.470
Um, is that you, Mizuki-chan?

15:21.470 --> 15:23.470
Senpai!

15:25.470 --> 15:27.060
It must be tough for you.

15:27.060 --> 15:28.350
Yeah, it must be.

15:29.850 --> 15:32.500
Things like that are painful, aren't they?

15:32.500 --> 15:34.110
Yeah, it must be painful.

15:36.110 --> 15:40.410
It would've been better if he'd said that he hated you, so you could just give up.

15:40.410 --> 15:42.990
But he can't, can he?

15:43.990 --> 15:49.240
In the end, I couldn't tell Renji-kun that I hated him.

15:49.240 --> 15:52.160
That was the one lie I couldn't tell.

15:52.160 --> 15:53.440
I see.

15:57.470 --> 15:58.380
Mizuki?

15:57.470 --> 15:58.380
Mizuki-chan?

15:58.380 --> 15:59.130
Huh?

15:59.130 --> 16:00.050
Um, yeah!

16:00.050 --> 16:01.970
It's just like you said!

16:01.970 --> 16:04.640
Geez, we're worried about you, okay?

16:05.600 --> 16:07.310
Sorry, I was thinking about something.

16:07.310 --> 16:10.810
Oh, right. I'm not sure if this will be of any use to you,

16:10.810 --> 16:12.810
but I wanted to give it to you, Mizuki-chan.

16:13.810 --> 16:19.080
For a dream to come true, you have to start out with a dream.

16:19.080 --> 16:20.740
With a dream?

16:20.740 --> 16:24.170
If you throw away your feelings, then nothing will happen.

16:24.170 --> 16:27.210
That's why you have to keep your feelings and never give up.

16:27.210 --> 16:31.160
Apparently, that's the first step towards making a dream reality.

16:31.160 --> 16:34.880
That's one of the things I remember every morning.

16:37.660 --> 16:39.170
What's this?

16:39.170 --> 16:42.310
It's a key to the rooftop of Otowa Academy.

16:42.310 --> 16:46.520
It's a charm I received from Himura-san, but I'll give it to you, Mizuki-chan.

16:46.520 --> 16:47.560
Are you all right with this?

16:47.560 --> 16:48.770
Yes.

16:48.770 --> 16:52.980
The charm has already blessed Renji-kun and me with its grace.

16:52.980 --> 16:54.480
W-Wait a second!

16:55.650 --> 16:58.730
Don't tell me... that key is the same as this one?

16:58.730 --> 17:00.750
Kei-senpai, what's that?

17:00.750 --> 17:03.710
A key to the rooftop of Otowa Academy in Japan.

17:03.710 --> 17:07.100
Tsutsumi-senpai gave it to me as a charm.

17:07.100 --> 17:08.370
You too, Kei-senpai?

17:08.370 --> 17:10.940
I don't need it anymore either.

17:10.940 --> 17:12.870
I'll give this to you as well, Mizuki.

17:21.890 --> 17:25.430
Is this a common charm in society?

17:26.710 --> 17:27.760
Who knows?

17:27.760 --> 17:30.890
But it ought to have double the effect now.

17:30.890 --> 17:35.480
Even if they're weak, they might really work now that you have two of them.

17:36.390 --> 17:40.320
I don't really get it, but thank you very much.

17:40.320 --> 17:41.690
Oh, yeah,

17:41.690 --> 17:44.840
while we're at it, can I make another request?

17:44.840 --> 17:45.480
Hm?

17:45.480 --> 17:48.580
Chihiro-senpai, can I have a sheet of that?

17:59.920 --> 18:01.920
Probably

18:03.810 --> 18:05.420
What's gotten into me?

18:05.990 --> 18:08.430
What am I scared of <i>now?</i>

18:12.220 --> 18:13.880
Isn't this great?

18:13.880 --> 18:15.730
I wanted to settle everything, didn't I?

18:15.730 --> 18:18.540
I finally wiped the slate clean.

18:18.540 --> 18:20.730
What am I scared of?

18:29.510 --> 18:32.020
The medicines that will extend my remaining days...

18:32.020 --> 18:33.450
Do I really have to take these pills?

18:34.350 --> 18:38.040
Do I really want to extend what remains of my life?

18:38.040 --> 18:40.520
Is that what I want?

18:42.070 --> 18:43.990
Of course not, right?

18:43.990 --> 18:46.220
There's no way in hell I'd will this on myself!

19:02.010 --> 19:03.820
I'm scared...

19:03.820 --> 19:05.490
of dying...

19:08.390 --> 19:10.480
What's wrong with me?

19:10.480 --> 19:12.710
What the hell is wrong?

19:12.710 --> 19:15.500
What am I frightened of?

19:15.690 --> 19:19.020
I've run away from everything I couldn't do, haven't I?

19:19.020 --> 19:21.750
Nothing will chase me anymore.

19:21.750 --> 19:24.500
Nothing will trouble me anymore.

19:24.500 --> 19:27.630
Do you truly believe you can run away from it?

19:27.630 --> 19:30.840
Do you truly believe you're not going to lose?

19:32.350 --> 19:36.600
Do you truly believe that life has winners and losers in the first place?

19:37.600 --> 19:41.860
Isn't thinking about victory or defeat itself an indicator of defeat?

19:42.860 --> 19:43.770
That's not it.

19:43.770 --> 19:44.860
It's not anything like that!

19:44.860 --> 19:47.880
You feel sad when you part with the one you love, because you love them.

19:47.880 --> 19:50.860
Or should you not fall in love in order not to feel sad?

19:50.860 --> 19:53.030
If you fall in love with them, then you get hurt.

19:53.030 --> 19:55.330
If they fall in love with you, then you don't.

19:56.260 --> 19:58.050
Yeah.

19:58.050 --> 19:59.510
And what's wrong with that?

19:59.510 --> 20:01.610
I've always been happy like that!

20:01.610 --> 20:03.500
Everything has been going well that way!

20:03.500 --> 20:06.350
Without hurting anyone... without being hurt by anyone...

20:06.350 --> 20:08.740
Everything has been going well!

20:08.740 --> 20:11.740
But then, why...

20:11.740 --> 20:14.260
Why is this so painful?

20:16.660 --> 20:18.850
Have I lost?

20:19.410 --> 20:21.420
I've run so much.

20:21.420 --> 20:24.300
I've reached a place where there's no one else.

20:24.300 --> 20:25.440
And I've lost?

20:28.280 --> 20:30.530
I'm scared.

20:30.530 --> 20:32.400
I'm alone.

20:32.400 --> 20:36.540
Without music, without my violin, and without the one I love.

20:36.540 --> 20:38.610
None of them are with me!

20:38.610 --> 20:40.040
No one is here with me!

20:40.320 --> 20:42.550
I'm scared!

20:42.550 --> 20:44.630
I'm all alone!

20:53.220 --> 20:53.340
letter of
challenge

21:32.430 --> 21:45.820
The shining wind calmly sways from gaps in the clouds.

21:46.400 --> 21:53.250
The echoing sounds sparkle.

21:53.370 --> 21:56.750
Even if it's a hope that was nearly lost,

21:57.000 --> 22:04.380
I should be able to find it again

22:06.680 --> 22:09.550
Holding firmly onto your sound,

22:10.180 --> 22:19.730
I don't let go of your hand joined with mine.

22:20.690 --> 22:26.530
Please don't forget the important things.

22:27.700 --> 22:34.200
A smile continues on into the future.

22:53.640 --> 22:54.560
What's up?

22:54.560 --> 22:57.520
I'm here to ask for some courage.

22:57.520 --> 22:59.060
Courage?

22:59.060 --> 22:59.940
From whom?

22:59.940 --> 23:01.810
From someone you don't know.

23:02.150 --> 23:05.070
There isn't anyone here that I don't know.

23:05.070 --> 23:08.150
Because she actually isn't here.

23:09.950 --> 23:12.910
This is for someone named Amamiya Yuko-san.

23:13.870 --> 23:19.120
Even though it would've been better to give this to her on the 25th.

23:19.120 --> 23:20.370
You're...

23:22.170 --> 23:22.920
You're...

23:25.840 --> 23:27.840
The past is remembered,

23:27.840 --> 23:30.680
and the fated meeting is considered.

23:30.680 --> 23:33.930
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:33.930 --> 23:35.890
Reunion.

23:35.890 --> 23:39.640
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
